From 9fef1ecd64bb5b95386d0b368126f74079bf522e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Assam Boudjelthia <assam.boudjelthia@qt.io>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:03:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Android: fix cross-container iterator in longPress word
 select

The backward word scan started at before.rbegin() but compared
against after.rend(), mixing reverse iterators from two different
containers. That is undefined behavior and could walk off the
start of before when the preceding text is all alphanumeric.
Compare against before.rend().

Backport of upstream qtbase 83876bf5500b to 6.9.3.

Fixes: QTBUG-148434
Change-Id: I9e000e9e98cfbf00a577d988d872e36d89bdc6eb
Reviewed-by: Ville Voutilainen <ville.voutilainen@qt.io>
---
 src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidinputcontext.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidinputcontext.cpp b/src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidinputcontext.cpp
index 2318a1f6..54d56f1c 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidinputcontext.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidinputcontext.cpp
@@ -861,7 +861,7 @@ void QAndroidInputContext::longPress(int x, int y)
             ++anchor;
         }
 
-        for (auto itch = before.rbegin(); itch != after.rend(); ++itch) {
+        for (auto itch = before.rbegin(); itch != before.rend(); ++itch) {
             if (!itch->isLetterOrNumber())
                 break;
             --cursor;
-- 
2.56.1

